# File Size & Directory Structure

## Hard limits

- **Max 200 lines per source file** (`.js`, `.jsx`, `.ts`, `.tsx`, `.css`, etc.)
- Do **not** add logic to a file that is already at or over 200 lines — split first
- Target function/component body: **≤ 60 lines**; extract helpers when larger

## When a file grows

1. Stop adding to the oversized file
2. Create a **feature directory** for related code
3. Split by responsibility (list / form / hooks / api / constants / modals)
4. Keep a thin page/entry file that only composes imports
5. One primary export per file

## Preferred layout

```text
src/features/<FeatureName>/
  constants.js
  api/
  domain/
  hooks/
  ui/
  index.js          # re-exports only
  README.md         # what lives where
```

Thin route pages stay in `src/pages/` and import from the feature.

## Naming

- Use **meaningful** file and directory names that describe ownership (e.g. `AttendeeSearchToolbar.jsx`, `useEBadgeJobs.js`)
- Prefer feature verbs/nouns over vague names (`utils`, `helpers`, `misc`, `common2`)
- Directory names: PascalCase feature folders (`Attendees/`), lowercase role folders (`hooks/`, `domain/`, `ui/`)

## Examples

- ❌ `src/pages/Attendees.jsx` (~1900 lines) — god file
- ✅ `src/features/Attendees/ui/AttendeesPage.jsx` + `AttendeeSearchToolbar.jsx` + `hooks/useAttendeeSearch.js` + …

## Before finishing any coding task

- [ ] No new/edited source file exceeds **200 lines**
- [ ] Related files live in one feature directory with meaningful names
- [ ] Oversized files were split before adding features
